{"id": "q0160", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4242962681, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": " Consider the transition between two forms of solid tin, $\\mathrm{Sn}(s$, gray $) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Sn}(s$, white $)$. The two phases are in equilibrium at 1 bar and $18^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The densities for gray and white tin are 5750 and $7280 \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~m}^{-3}$, respectively, and the molar entropies for gray and white tin are 44.14 and $51.18 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$, respectively. Calculate the temperature at which the two phases are in equilibrium at 350. bar.\n\nA. 5.2 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nB. -7.8 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nC. -3.5 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nD. 0.0 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nE. 21.4 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nF. -10.0 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nG. 10.0 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nH. -15.2 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nI. -25.0 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\nJ. 13.7 $^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0160.wav", "input_sha256": "be940326112268860e32271ab7300efe2524c9efaeb7d08c0a1020fb54e3ba81", "input_samples": 949600, "input_s": 59.35, "n_real_chunks": 60, "score": 0.7997, "act": 0.9972, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "E, 21.4 kelvin (the equilibrium temperature shifts downward by about 21.4 K, to roughly 269.7 K or −3.4 °C)", "expert_answer": "**E, 21.4 kelvin**  \n(the equilibrium temperature shifts downward by about 21.4 K, to roughly **269.7 K** or **−3.4 °C**)", "transcript": "Consider the transition between two forms of solid tin, gray tin, written mathrm s, and white