"status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.962, "last_real_feed_done": 3.031, "onset": 4.716, "gate_read_done": 4.716, "fire": 4.716, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.716, "stall_note": 4.717, "stall_first_pcm": 5.464, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.464, "expert_req": 4.717, "expert_resp": 6.755, "relay_synth_start": 6.755, "relay_first_pcm": 7.399, "relay_synth_end": 7.609, "first_any_pcm": 4.716, "first_answer_pcm": 7.399, "session_end": 7.734}, "ttfa_answer_s": 4.437, "ttfa_any_s": 1.753}
{"id": "q0421", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3913699200, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0421.wav", "input_sha256": "a04bc3b64cacbe5bddeaa1d889dc260b0d7986d64c1d92ca2a6b5209969d4371", "input_samples": 67400, "input_s": 4.213, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.3168, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The best iron swing and best driver swing are different because the clubs are designed to do different jobs. Iron swing: hit down and compress the ball With an iron, the goal is to strike the ball first, then the turf. Simple setup comparison In short: swing irons to compress the ball; swing driver to launch the ball.", "expert_answer": "The **best iron swing** and **best driver swing** are different because the clubs are designed to do different jobs.\n\n## Iron swing: hit down and compress the ball\nWith an iron, the goal is to strike the **ball first, then the turf**.\n\nKey points:\n- **Ball position:** More centered, or slightly forward of center depending on the iron.\n- **Weight/pressure:** Slightly more pressure on the lead foot at impact.\n- **Angle of attack:** Slightly **downward**.\n- **Hands at impact:** Hands ahead of the ball, creating shaft lean.\n- **Divot:** Ideally after the ball, not before it.\n- **Goal:** Compress the ball against the clubface and control distance/trajectory.\n\nA good iron thought:  \n**“Ball first, then ground.”**\n\n## Driver swing: sweep up on the ball\nWith a driver, the ball is on a tee, so the goal is usually to launch it high with low spin by hitting it on the **upswing** or with a shallow angle of attack.\n\nKey points:\n- **Ball position:** Forward, near the lead heel.\n- **Stance:** Wider than with irons.\n- **Spine tilt:** Slight tilt away from the target at address.\n- **Angle of attack:** Level to slightly **upward**.\n- **Hands at impact:** Less forward shaft lean than with irons.\n- **Divot:** No divot; you are sweeping the ball off the tee.\n- **Goal:** Maximize launch, speed, and carry distance.\n\nA good driver thought:  \n**“Sweep it off the tee.”**\n\n## Main difference\n- **Irons:** Hit **down** on the ball to create compression and take a divot after impact.\n- **Driver:** Hit **up or shallow** to launch the ball with speed and distance.\n\n## Simple setup comparison\n\n| Club | Ball Position | Angle of Attack | Contact Goal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Iron | Center to slightly forward | Downward | Ball first, then turf |\n| Driver | Forward near lead heel | Upward/shallow | Sweep off tee |\n\nIn short: **swing irons to compress the ball; swing driver to launch the ball.**", "transcript": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.\n", "asr_s": 0.55, "expert_s": 8.57, "expert_input_samples": 67400, "expert_input_s": 4.213, "expert_input_sha256": "a04bc3b64cacbe5bddeaa1d889dc260b0d7986d64c1d92ca2a6b5209969d4371", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 7.71, "relay_synth_ms": 11468, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 154, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 154, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0421_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "eb74d8744f9258919b0301405cf264650d2b70e3be30375fa56d9fb073e971c8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 21.72}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0421_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "cb3f405c997303fa01ff977c2f3efd2cc9c96124787ca4717b171e3edcebb7f8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0421_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "1a2bf1bffed9f7a524ac8699589af6bbc57772991e51c374070b2f14e5ac9eab", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.069, 1.125, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.07, 2.124, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.075, 3.13, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.069, 4.124, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 4.213, 4.283, 4.771, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.213, 5.439, 6.177, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 4.213, "last_real_feed_done": 4.283, "onset": 4.771, "gate_read_done": 4.771, "fire": 4.771, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.771, "stall_note": 4.772, "stall_first_pcm": 5.367, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 6.177, "expert_req": 4.772, "expert_resp": 13.886, "relay_synth_start": 13.887, "relay_first_pcm": 14.67, "relay_synth_end": 25.355, "first_any_pcm": 4.771, "first_answer_pcm": 14.67, "session_end": 26.159}, "ttfa_answer_s": 10.458, "ttfa_any_s": 0.558}
{"id": "q0437", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 423549940, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "What is the GE Dash 8-32BWH", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0437.wav", "input_sha256": "2dc2a840be5f0352a563cb1c42b5bd13d8f51dc774faad4c7fdec25a045c5a57", "input_samples": 34600, "input_s": 2.163, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.9057, "act": 0.9962, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The only identifiable reference I found for GE-832BH appears to be a historic vehicle/registration listing: 832BH is listed as the registration/license for a 1959 Lister “Knobbly” Jaguar, chassis BHL103, associated with Derek Wilkinson / John Bekaert, noted as possibly a trade plate and ex–Peter Whitehead. (vasmel.com) So, GE-832BH is likely referring to a Lister Knobbly Jaguar race car listing/registration, not a modern product model number.", "expert_answer": "The only identifiable reference I found for **GE-832BH** appears to be a **historic vehicle/registration listing**: **832BH** is listed as the registration/license for a **1959 Lister “Knobbly” Jaguar**, chassis **BHL103**, associated with **Derek Wilkinson / John Bekaert**, noted as possibly a trade plate and ex–Peter Whitehead. ([vasmel.com](https://vasmel.com/Lic-GreatBritain.htm?utm_source=openai))\n\nSo, **GE-832BH is likely referring to a Lister Knobbly Jaguar race car listing/registration, not a modern product model number**.", "transcript": "What is the GE-832BH?\n", "asr_s": 0.45, "expert_s": 9.61, "expert_input_samples": 34600, "expert_input_s": 2.163, "expert_input_sha256": "2dc2a840be5f0352a563cb1c42b5bd13d8f51dc774faad4c7fdec25a045c5a57", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 8.952, "relay_synth_ms": 20089, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 374, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 374, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0437_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "dbc3fc57a9cec145a6b95a9e866b4e3d581ab3280b643e4cf43f6ab5fb6e3be5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 33.52}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0437_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "8d65600f59173a629208955c3f66077195294a2340f1872bc8532a7b040ba864", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0437_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "9abc8b32bacbb7b315b8a33e73322a9f856257ca72084be2ad042e12eefbd6a7", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.68}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.066, 1.122, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.068, 2.122, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.163, 2.23, 2.286, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.163, 3.232, 3.948, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.162, 4.605, 5.053, 0, 16320, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.163, "last_real_feed_done": 2.23, "onset": 3.948, "gate_read_done": 3.949, "fire": 3.949, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.948, "stall_note": 3.95, "stall_first_pcm": 4.537, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.053, "expert_req": 3.949, "expert_resp": 14.005, "relay_synth_start": 14.006, "relay_first_pcm": 14.935, "relay_synth_end": 34.095, "first_any_pcm": 3.948, "first_answer_pcm": 14.935, "session_end": 34.503}, "ttfa_answer_s": 12.772, "ttfa_any_s": 1.786}
{"id": "q0461", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2368375428, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "how do you rate strength of tornado", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0461.wav", "input_sha256": "b46c1045cfba15c0cb217bb44e049ff9d6079a98469671437f97f490ad9db590", "input_samples": 32000, "input_s": 2.0, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.2193, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Tornado strength is rated using the Enhanced Fujita (EF) Scale, which estimates wind speed based on the damage a tornado causes. The scale runs from EF0 to EF5: EF0: 65–85 mph — light damage , EF1: 86–110 mph — moderate damage , EF2: 111–135 mph — considerable damage , EF3: 136–165 mph — severe damage , EF4: 166–200 mph — devastating damage , EF5: over 200 mph — incredible damage So, tornadoes are rated after the event by surveying damage, not usually by directly measuring wind speed.", "expert_answer": "Tornado strength is rated using the **Enhanced Fujita (EF) Scale**, which estimates wind speed based on the **damage** a tornado causes.\n\nThe scale runs from **EF0 to EF5**:\n\n- **EF0:** 65–85 mph — light damage  \n- **EF1:** 86–110 mph — moderate damage  \n- **EF2:** 111–135 mph — considerable damage  \n- **EF3:** 136–165 mph — severe damage  \n- **EF4:** 166–200 mph — devastating damage  \n- **EF5:** over 200 mph — incredible damage  \n\nSo, tornadoes are rated **after the event** by surveying damage, not usually by directly measuring wind speed.", "transcript": "How do you rate strength of tornado?\n", "asr_s": 0.76, "expert_s": 3.1, "expert_input_samples": 32000, "expert_input_s": 2.0, "expert_input_sha256": "b46c1045cfba15c0cb217bb44e049ff9d6079a98469671437f97f490ad9db590", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.069, "relay_synth_ms": 27168, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0461_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "2acd1964bab33904cbd8269889accd92d3f061ec9d480ce2d32119eb570ffc71", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 49.52}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0461_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "3966f005bd817aff6055e4fc541e07a674fda02c14ae2fab7c6e29e85bfc2679", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0461_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "fb1fad92030661fc3ec8049b194c2e913ee663b213f85f5257d1b4d34a3ecf94", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.072, 1.131, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.073, 2.13, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 3.0, 3.072, 3.132, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 4.0, 4.074, 4.593, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.0, "last_real_feed_done": 2.073, "onset": 4.593, "gate_read_done": 4.593, "fire": 4.593, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.593, "stall_note": 4.595, "stall_first_pcm": 5.382, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.382, "expert_req": 4.594, "expert_resp": 8.451, "relay_synth_start": 8.452, "relay_first_pcm": 9.252, "relay_synth_end": 35.62, "first_any_pcm": 4.593, "first_answer_pcm": 9.252, "session_end": 36.029}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.252, "ttfa_any_s": 2.593}
